          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ddef828be7188750173133a44288cf0100b1ecb442d656e9b6ad4367cc6fb253:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_829e09e66ec44c648dd668e55c99b0d4",
      "statement": "aws-reboot and aws-terminate both declare only ServiceEC2 in RequiredServices because their pre-write ownership check (DescribeInstances) and the mutation itself are both EC2 calls, so a write needs no client a read does not already have.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/actions/aws_ec2.go#L109-L111",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9001e922d1c03cc5f1700e733cbeb9df62572d7bb5a1cb29e737e297ef300a45:"
