          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:594d93947424047349d87f5df9d8ff4251a75e181962441636f3d73d5b460154:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/executor/aws.go#L64-L75",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f35281a45792b54063ea2594bec0e23bdfe6db4846274d674fa3d7f3a2077dd2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0320d0b7969c44f79aef403cc162beaa",
      "statement": "authorization.AWSAuthorizer.Authorize enforces two independent, fail-closed allowlists: AllowedRegions gates every AWS request (read or write) and AllowedOperations gates only writes (non-empty Operation); both default to empty, meaning an unconfigured deployment denies all AWS reads and all AWS writes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/authorization/aws.go#L18-L36",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6152ee501796a1e3bc62c148c848323d6242ca6000df9913b9f793388bb8cc9e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/authorization/aws.go#L79-L124",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:64674c6ee309eabd578e3bbd280f26a20a8c4e28c0861cc63f7666a11f810613:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a1a44121485c468fa9cce7bae4767434",
      "statement": "aws_write.go's requireClusterInstance enforces per-instance ownership for reboot/terminate by describing the target instance and requiring the kubernetes.io/cluster/<infraID>=owned tag, refusing the write if the tag is absent, the value is 'shared' instead of 'owned', or the target's InfraID could not be resolved at all; this bounds a write's blast radius to the cluster rather than the whole AWS account the credentials can reach.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/actions/aws_write.go#L24-L94",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7f5ac96daa580a365a7a38fbc85149e9983a5e79f47485fb2635e52849615983:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0b6ab7e560364b4792c919de4a8219af",
      "statement": "awsapi.ClientProvider.DefaultRegion and ClusterInfraID both return an empty string without an error when the provider cannot determine an answer, and callers (the authorizer, and requireClusterInstance) must treat an empty answer as unproven/denied rather than as permission to proceed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/actions/aws_write.go#L54-L60",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6fc50ccdb630771235d82beb318b16027205f26eae035be03ea0ec74020d9a65:"
