    {
      "id": "claim_5cb654b35d34442caa7dba906d007943",
      "statement": "awsapi.StaticProvider builds every client from one fixed StaticConfig (region, static credentials, EndpointURL override, and a single configured InfraID) and ignores clusterID entirely, so every execution reaches the same AWS account regardless of which cluster is named; it must not be used in production for per-cluster isolation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/awsapi/static.go#L13-L67",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cbd972870c24178616214e5a96320e137e23a97f8b61dc98b1fbdb342b1f42e0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_aa2185cc6a5842808a92fc85ae8ec4d0",
      "statement": "cmd/server/main.go selects awsapi.StaticProvider when ROSA_TA_AWS_ENDPOINT_URL is set (an endpoint override can only sensibly mean a local emulator such as LocalStack) and otherwise selects awsapi.CloudCredentialsProvider, logging a warning in the static case; the server fails startup if neither an endpoint override nor a usable OCM client is available.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://cmd/server/main.go#L275-L321",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f4256f5b0f794a3206aacb47932c211fdbc735f513a1b20ecfb9ab1a6f7a26ad:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d5dd4721c0da47ba812493cde8971772",
      "statement": "awsapi.CloudCredentialsProvider resolves a cluster's AWS account by caching the OCM cluster record (ClusterCacheTTL, default 5 minutes), confirming the cluster's cloud provider is aws, then calling backplane-cli's GetCloudCredentials to walk the SRE assume-role chain from the payer account into the customer's own account and obtain short-lived STS credentials scoped to it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/awsapi/credentials.go#L253-L300",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:72ffa79000eb892e3a213e98a15c7c6db55338240e774760c413f94e2a04a0c2:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/awsapi/credentials.go#L29-L33",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6bceab309390caf3296a379d722b10bbfb504d67142ff85a95a5593e4f688c77:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/awsapi/credentials.go#L302-L334",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:32baf576787024a418a01dcc86bd04f520f45d3c281510ae5536846c7948ec90:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/awsapi/credentials.go#L69-L123",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ca7d5efb8976345ffabd1cb0ed25b67bd2ea6a215db16e943eba1796b44b8a43:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_725f09024482432fba85b8250a45f54f",
      "statement": "CloudCredentialsProvider fetches AWS credentials fresh on every execution rather than caching them (unlike the cluster record), so revoking a cluster's backplane access grant takes effect on the very next request; it also requires the server's egress to be within OCM's trusted IP range or routed through AWSProxyURL, since the assume-role chain only grants credentials to trusted callers.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/awsapi/credentials.go#L161-L213",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d3eb26e6e9257bbba003b4b0cfd1b0fb32b87a6434047bd151382eb28a871173:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/awsapi/credentials.go#L80-L105",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:be228a475dac3cba037aced72df020284015c35cfa878ad8da43422942a4503a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c98e305894ca4c3b9059ff2f71ce420c",
      "statement": "CloudCredentialsProvider's backplane-cli credential call accepts no context.Context, so awaitCredentials runs it in a goroutine and returns early if the execution context is cancelled first; the result channel is buffered so the abandoned goroutine can still send and exit once the call eventually completes, bounding (not eliminating) the worker-goroutine leak a slow backplane/STS call would otherwise cause.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/awsapi/credentials.go#L220-L251",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0736533a36df79e9986cb80fc6ba84ea344007e0e3a81fc090be7e1fb9ab6765:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6ef939d8395c4af19c0c74a62ae541e8",
      "statement": "NewCloudCredentialsProvider takes an OCMConnectionFunc (a func() (*ocmsdk.Connection, error)) rather than a single *ocmsdk.Connection, because the server outlives any one OCM connection's finite-lived token; resolving a fresh connection per credential fetch lets the owner hand back a refreshed connection without awsapi needing to know refreshing occurs. cmd/server/main.go calls ocmClient.Connection() once at startup only to fail fast, then passes the accessor function itself to the provider.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://cmd/server/main.go#L305-L320",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7e2057533ae5d81ebc19c73a18a5596f8eb4b2d37cfc3f7c430b0a2111ddf61e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/awsapi/credentials.go#L262-L268",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e00d7d7897a1d4d26a35f68bda48282a9e80bff9cc90f6ca8b96b06f046817fb:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/awsapi/credentials.go#L59-L67",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a18a514048696aada3cfc330df89d57075a34f11375a9804b0c38d1dc7bfffad:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6c351c689b48477d93eac9f4b6350f7c",
      "statement": "AWSScope.DeriveTarget calls ClientProvider.DefaultRegion before authorization runs for every AWS request, and calls ClusterInfraID (storing it on AWSTarget.InfraID) only when the action is an AWSWriteAction; both resolutions happen from the same authoritative cluster lookup rather than from caller-supplied params, and a failure to resolve either aborts the execution as an executor.Failure.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/executor/aws.go#L33-L89",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4fb645f9b60f8c19d1e488925b1ea793455858e1e747c77ac0b990613e127bd6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_59af842324df46059fe95dda20fb1c43",
      "statement": "The region AWSScope resolves and authorizes a request against is exactly the region used for the subsequent GetClients call and the action's AWS calls, because callers never supply a region param themselves — a caller-sent 'region' param is rejected as an unrecognized param rather than honored.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/executor/aws.go#L33-L54",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d7667665c696d817b91412d4b1f4dd1a5413e9048a06e4ffed2332a28c572294:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d1e7e12fcbe04722bfa9778fce7f6174",
      "statement": "aws-get is a generic read action driven by the awsResources registry mapping resource names to an awsapi.Service, a describe function, an id-support mode (optional/required/unsupported), and an accepted-params list; a request naming an unrecognized param is rejected outright rather than silently ignored, preventing a caller's filter expectation from being silently dropped.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/actions/aws_get.go#L179-L213",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:93552be390610888a5d4f71b956e2e39f4e29f5ab638aab2e559966611cb15d4:"
